---
description: Thin screens — bind API results directly, no client reshape
globs: frontend/src/app/screens/**/*.ts,frontend/src/app/services/**/*.ts
alwaysApply: false
---

# Direct API bind

Screens bind service results as returned. Do not reshape lists in the component unless the UI truly needs it.

```ts
// ❌ BAD — unnecessary client sort / copy
const rows = await this.taxService.search({});
this.taxList.set(rows.slice().sort((a, b) => a.name.localeCompare(b.name)));

// ✅ GOOD — set what the API returned
this.taxList.set(await this.taxService.search({}));
```

- No mappers, DTO→view-model copies, or cosmetic `slice()`/`sort()`/`map()` on load.
- Filter/search in the UI is fine (e.g. local search box on an already-loaded list).
- Sort/filter belongs on the API when the list must be ordered for everyone.
- Services wrap POST bodies with `actionRequest(item)` (`{ Item, securitytoken }` — InfyPOS `ActionRequest<T>`). Screens still bind the response body as-is (`T[]` / `T` / `boolean`).
- Keep screen API calls straightforward: `await service…`, then bind / navigate. No extra ok/id/ErrorMessage branches, duplicate error toasts, or catch that only re-notifies — HTTP errors are handled by interceptors.
- Login `/token` is form-urlencoded OAuth — not `ActionRequest`.
